---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About Rex Autistikōn Labs and the Rex Autistikon Research Foundation.">
  <section class="py-16">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-8">About</h1>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-4">Rex Autistikōn Labs</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
        Rex Autistikōn Labs is an independent research initiative operating under the Rex Autistikon Research Foundation, Inc. We investigate the hypothesis that chronic mechanical restriction within specific sensor-rich myofascial and visceral interfaces contributes to altered afferent signaling in neurodevelopmental conditions.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 mt-12 mb-4">Our Approach</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
        We integrate biotensegrity theory, fascia as a sensory organ, mechanotransduction, viscoelastic signal filtering, and predictive coding frameworks to generate testable, mechanism-based hypotheses. Our work prioritizes open science, mathematical formalization, and clear experimental pathways.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 mt-12 mb-4">Legal Structure</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
        Rex Autistikon Research Foundation, Inc. is a 501(c)(3) public charity.
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-lg text-slate-600 space-y-2 mb-6">
        <li>EIN: 42-3220323</li>
        <li>Address: 1485 Fouraker Rd #2402, Jacksonville, FL 32221, United States</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 mt-12 mb-4">Founder</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
        Hai Young Kim — independent researcher focused on the biomechanics of sensory and interoceptive signaling in neurodevelopmental conditions.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>